<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:25:55 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>猴子养宠物吗？研究发现灵长类动物与其他动物物种（从老鼠到鹿）之间存在广泛的相互作用</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/do-monkeys-keep-pets-study-finds-widespread-primate-interactions-with-other-animal-species-from-mice-to-deer-180989356/</link><description>科学家表示，这种社会行为可能揭示了人类饲养宠物特征的进化根源，从照顾到宽容和好奇心。但这和养猫养狗不一样</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:22:41 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/do-monkeys-keep-pets-study-finds-widespread-primate-interactions-with-other-animal-species-from-mice-to-deer-180989356/</guid></item><item><title>这种新批准的嗜睡症药物是第一个针对睡眠障碍的根本原因而不是其症状的药物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-newly-approved-narcolepsy-drug-is-the-first-to-target-the-sleep-disorders-root-cause-rather-than-its-symptoms-180989362/</link><description>美国食品和药物管理局刚刚批准了一种名为 Orzeyful 的药物，用于治疗成人 1 型发作性睡病。这种情况是由产生食欲素的脑细胞丧失引起的，食欲素是调节睡眠-觉醒周期的重要化学物质</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 19:18:35 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-newly-approved-narcolepsy-drug-is-the-first-to-target-the-sleep-disorders-root-cause-rather-than-its-symptoms-180989362/</guid></item><item><title>拯救一棵在革命战争中幸存下来的 300 岁古树的斗争</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/inside-fight-to-save-300-year-old-tree-that-survived-revolutionary-war-battle-180989357/</link><description>树木学家正在努力保护南卡罗来纳州尤托斯普林斯战场公园 (Eutaw Springs Battlefield Park) 的 45 英尺高的活橡树。这棵历史树在 50 年前的一次雷击中受损</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 15:50:28 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/inside-fight-to-save-300-year-old-tree-that-survived-revolutionary-war-battle-180989357/</guid></item><item><title>窃贼潜入博物馆并在夜间将其带走几个月后，在一个纸板箱中发现了价值 1000 万美元的被盗杰作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/stolen-masterpieces-worth-10-million-discovered-in-a-cardboard-box-months-after-thieves-snuck-into-a-museum-and-whisked-them-away-into-the-night-180989358/</link><description>塞尚、雷诺阿和马蒂斯的艺术作品在今年早些时候的一次三分钟抢劫中消失了。现在，警方逮捕了与意大利北部入室盗窃案有关的五名嫌疑人</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 15:24:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/stolen-masterpieces-worth-10-million-discovered-in-a-cardboard-box-months-after-thieves-snuck-into-a-museum-and-whisked-them-away-into-the-night-180989358/</guid></item><item><title>西非附近的这些珊瑚礁长期以来被认为已经死亡。科学家刚刚发现它们还活着并且充满生命</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-coral-reefs-off-west-africa-were-long-presumed-dead-scientists-just-found-them-alive-and-teeming-with-life-180989350/</link><description>20 世纪 60 年代的鱼类调查在贝宁国家附近发现了专家认为是死亡的珊瑚礁屏障。几十年后，研究人员乘坐小渔船出发，利用声纳测绘、水下无人机勘测和固定录像机对其进行调查</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 14:34:49 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-coral-reefs-off-west-africa-were-long-presumed-dead-scientists-just-found-them-alive-and-teeming-with-life-180989350/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，中年时避免这三种血管健康风险因素可帮助您将痴呆症延迟约 13 年</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/avoiding-these-three-vascular-health-risk-factors-in-midlife-can-help-you-delay-dementia-for-about-13-years-study-suggests-180989354/</link><description>高血压、糖尿病和吸烟是痴呆症的三个主要可改变危险因素。新研究跟踪了超过 12,000 名参与者，以量化在中年时期避免部分或全部认知功能可以获得多少年的健康认知功能</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/avoiding-these-three-vascular-health-risk-factors-in-midlife-can-help-you-delay-dementia-for-about-13-years-study-suggests-180989354/</guid></item><item><title>当西西里人涌入宗教节日时，窃贼闯入附近的博物馆并偷走了四幅文艺复兴时期的画作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/as-sicilians-flocked-to-religious-festival-thieves-broke-into-nearby-museum-stole-four-renaissance-paintings-180989352/</link><description>失踪的作品包括安东内罗·达·梅西纳 (Antonello da Messina) 创作的 15 世纪祭坛画中的三幅嵌板，以及该艺术家的一幅双面虔诚画作</description><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 19:36:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/as-sicilians-flocked-to-religious-festival-thieves-broke-into-nearby-museum-stole-four-renaissance-paintings-180989352/</guid></item><item><title>天文学家可能首次在早期宇宙中发现了一个带有三个巨大黑洞的星系</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-first-astronomers-may-have-spotted-a-galaxy-in-the-early-universe-with-three-behemoth-black-holes-180989344/</link><description>星系的光大约需要 125 亿年才能到达詹姆斯·韦伯太空望远镜，这意味着该仪器在大爆炸 10 亿年多一点后才看到黑洞。其中两个黑洞似乎正在合并，这说明了物体是如何生长的</description><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 19:13:48 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-first-astronomers-may-have-spotted-a-galaxy-in-the-early-universe-with-three-behemoth-black-holes-180989344/</guid></item><item><title>动物什么时候开始生育后代？这个 2.36 亿年前的化石可能会改写哺乳动物的进化史</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-did-animals-start-giving-birth-to-live-young-this-236-million-year-old-fossil-might-rewrite-mammals-evolutionary-history-180989343/</link><description>在哺乳动物祖先身上发现的骨骼特征表明，该生物在新生儿时相对较大，更符合活产生物的大小，而不是从蛋中孵化出来的生物的大小。尽管如此，它只提供了间接证据</description><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 16:23:49 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-did-animals-start-giving-birth-to-live-young-this-236-million-year-old-fossil-might-rewrite-mammals-evolutionary-history-180989343/</guid></item><item><title>这对夫妇在他们的后院发现了埋藏着一个 150 磅重的神秘雕塑。现在，他们正试图找出是谁制造的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-couple-found-a-mysterious-150-pound-sculpture-buried-in-their-backyard-now-theyre-trying-to-figure-out-who-made-it-180989347/</link><description>格雷格·加特伍德 (Greg Gatwood) 和朱迪·吉特尔森 (Judy Gittelsohn) 五月份在旧金山的房产中发现了一尊巨大的石灰岩半身像后，在过去的几个月里一直试图揭开其背后的故事</description><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:33:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-couple-found-a-mysterious-150-pound-sculpture-buried-in-their-backyard-now-theyre-trying-to-figure-out-who-made-it-180989347/</guid></item><item><title>家长们，听着：推着婴儿车跑步可能会让您不太容易因过度使用而受伤</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/listen-up-parents-running-with-a-stroller-might-make-you-less-prone-to-overuse-injuries-180989345/</link><description>跑步者经常会遇到胫骨夹板、跑步膝和足底筋膜炎等病症，这些病症会导致脚跟底部疼痛。但推婴儿车的车把似乎会让你的体重分布不同</description><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/listen-up-parents-running-with-a-stroller-might-make-you-less-prone-to-overuse-injuries-180989345/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，Covid-19 可以重新唤醒体内休眠的病毒，这可能会加剧呼吸道疾病的症状</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/covid-19-can-reawaken-dormant-viruses-in-the-body-which-might-worsen-symptoms-of-the-respiratory-illness-study-suggests-180989322/</link><description>大多数人体内都携带一种休眠病毒，例如引起单核细胞增多症或“接吻病”的疱疹病毒。一项新的研究暗示，Covid-19 会触发它们的重新激活，这可能会使症状恶化并增加长期感染 Covid-19 的风险</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:06:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/covid-19-can-reawaken-dormant-viruses-in-the-body-which-might-worsen-symptoms-of-the-respiratory-illness-study-suggests-180989322/</guid></item><item><title>一名中世纪男子的受伤让一位考古学家想起了现代车祸受害者。原来它们是英国投石机的作品</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-medieval-mans-injuries-reminded-one-archaeologist-of-modern-day-car-crash-victims-they-turned-out-to-be-the-work-of-an-english-trebuchet-180989346/</link><description>在苏格兰出土的一具骨架很可能属于爱德华一世 1304 年围攻斯特灵城堡期间被高速射弹击中的一名士兵。该男子160多处骨折</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 19:49:12 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-medieval-mans-injuries-reminded-one-archaeologist-of-modern-day-car-crash-victims-they-turned-out-to-be-the-work-of-an-english-trebuchet-180989346/</guid></item><item><title>Schlitz 啤酒是一种标志性的中西部啤酒，177 年后在芝加哥干涸。然而，它的遗产远远超出了品脱玻璃杯的范畴</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/schlitz-beer-an-iconic-midwestern-pour-officially-runs-dry-in-chicago-after-177-years-180989342/</link><description>啤酒在芝加哥大火、1893 年世界博览会和现代建筑中发挥了重要作用，对风城的影响是不可否认的</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 18:05:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/schlitz-beer-an-iconic-midwestern-pour-officially-runs-dry-in-chicago-after-177-years-180989342/</guid></item><item><title>天文学家凝视早期宇宙，可能发现了一种新型天体：黑洞恒星</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/astronomers-peered-at-the-early-universe-and-may-have-discovered-a-new-kind-of-celestial-object-black-hole-stars-180989334/</link><description>自从詹姆斯·韦伯太空望远镜于 2022 年开始收集数据以来，它发现了一些被称为小红点的令人费解的物体。一项新研究表明它们可能是具有恒星某些特征的巨大黑洞</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:47:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/astronomers-peered-at-the-early-universe-and-may-have-discovered-a-new-kind-of-celestial-object-black-hole-stars-180989334/</guid></item><item><title>历史悠久的潜艇修复揭示了与二战期间沉没的失落姐妹船的隐藏联系</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/historic-submarine-restoration-reveals-a-hidden-connection-to-a-lost-sister-ship-that-sank-during-world-war-ii-180989340/</link><description>在“银赛德”号航空母舰上工作的专家发现了一个似乎是为它的姊妹舰“扳机”号航空母舰设计的泄洪阀。 1945年3月28日该船在东海沉没</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:01:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/historic-submarine-restoration-reveals-a-hidden-connection-to-a-lost-sister-ship-that-sank-during-world-war-ii-180989340/</guid></item><item><title>这就是为什么这些雄性蜘蛛在交配时通过翻筋斗进入雌性的尖牙来牺牲自己</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/heres-why-these-male-spiders-sacrifice-themselves-by-somersaulting-into-females-fangs-while-mating-180989337/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，即使是奇怪、复杂的动物行为也可能有相对简单的遗传基础</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/heres-why-these-male-spiders-sacrifice-themselves-by-somersaulting-into-females-fangs-while-mating-180989337/</guid></item><item><title>这本图书馆的书已经过期 150 年了。对于刚归还书的人来说幸运的是，图书馆员不会强制收取 20,000 美元的滞纳金</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-library-book-was-150-years-overdue-fortunately-for-the-man-who-just-returned-it-librarians-wont-be-enforcing-a-20000-late-fee-180989339/</link><description>自 1870 年代以来，澳大利亚图书馆很可能就失踪了《雅典古物》。工作人员表示，它的恢复是“一个不太可能的生存（书籍）和救赎（借阅者）的故事”</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 11:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-library-book-was-150-years-overdue-fortunately-for-the-man-who-just-returned-it-librarians-wont-be-enforcing-a-20000-late-fee-180989339/</guid></item><item><title>肉类并不是促使早期人类进化出更大大脑的唯一食物。糖可能也促进了器官的增大</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meat-wasnt-the-only-food-that-drove-early-humans-to-evolve-bigger-brains-sugar-may-have-fueled-the-organs-enlargement-too-180989335/</link><description>科学家们研究了四百万年的古人类饮食。他们发现，在烹饪之前，天然糖可能以葡萄糖的形式为正在发育的大脑提供能量，使淀粉类食物更容易消化</description><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 20:27:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meat-wasnt-the-only-food-that-drove-early-humans-to-evolve-bigger-brains-sugar-may-have-fueled-the-organs-enlargement-too-180989335/</guid></item><item><title>著名作曲家诞辰 270 周年数月后，萨尔茨堡 200 多尊莫扎特金色雕像被盗</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/more-than-200-golden-mozart-statuettes-stolen-from-salzburg-months-after-famed-composers-270th-birthday-180989332/</link><description>奥地利公共艺术装置盗窃案并不是作曲家微型雕像第一次被盗</description><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2026 19:07:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/more-than-200-golden-mozart-statuettes-stolen-